# Evidence behind the quoted numbers

Complete SQLite and native MySQL main-fixture grades pass on the measured
development snapshots below. The renamed second fixture also passes, but the
complete mod-write probe still fails and requires further fixes. This file
records the source, runtime, reference, result and limits of each measurement.

The other documents also contain observations outside these fixture grades.
The earlier failing comparison and its diagnostic re-check are recorded in
full in [KNOWN-COMPARISON-FAILURE.md](KNOWN-COMPARISON-FAILURE.md), and the
export build check is stated in [README.md](README.md). The remaining ones
are development observations with no record in this package, labelled as such
where they appear: the hosted RichText match and the Ruby view-cache runs in
[DEPLOYMENT.md](DEPLOYMENT.md), the snapshot-and-restore checks in
docs/handover/MIGRATION.md, and the hosted comparisons and the Linux
recovery run in [UNTESTED-INPUTS.md](UNTESTED-INPUTS.md). They are not graded
results.

Each measurement describes its named development snapshot, not every later
combined source or export. HANDOVER-MANIFEST.json identifies the exported
source; that artifact needs its own recorded checks. Current results below
name source commits; the older sections retain their original tree/source
records. Development Git history and complete machine-local receipts are not
redistributed, so those historical objects cannot be checked from this package
alone. The recorded summaries and shipped fixture manifests preserve the
reference and comparison context without treating a private push as release
acceptance.

The reference runtime is Ruby 3.2.3 on the project's Linux VM, running stock
Decko 0.20.0 / card 1.110.0. The fixture's committed recorded Ruby outputs for
synthetic-v1 were captured there on 2026-11-03 (`ruby 3.2.3
[aarch64-linux-gnu]`), over the fixture's committed deck, and a second
complete capture there differed only in random slot ids.

Each result states the reference it was measured against. Current SQLite
grades use the 2026-11-03 Ruby 3.2.3 capture, and the native MySQL grade uses
the fresh Ruby 3.2.3 MySQL capture described below. The two earlier
synthetic-v1 results were graded against the
recording it replaced, a 2026-10-08 capture taken on Windows with Ruby
3.3.12, which differs from it only in the order of class tokens (678 of 1,752
render operations, absorbed by rule N3) and in random slot ids (rule N1). The
51 browser journeys were compared with a live Ruby 3.2.3 server on a Linux
machine. The two database matrix results are engine-level tests with no Ruby
comparison.

